these people have recently heard prime  minister abdullah the first to hold the  position following sudan's 2018  revolution has resigned and many in the  country are divided on his departure  departure is a big loss to the nation he  had made a lot of achievements and  brought progress to sudan but the  military were the reason he was unable  to move forward on so many issues the  military is the reason we're in this  crisis  it doesn't make a difference just like  he doesn't make a difference if he stays  hamdock no longer serves the demands of  the people on the street he legitimized  a takeover and blessed what they have  done and this was much less than what  the people of sudan have been calling  for  hamduk was sworn in in 2019  after the overthrow of long-time  president ahmad al-bashir he was picked  by the coalition known as the forces of  freedom and change to lead sudan's  transition to democracy the coalition  represented the protest movement that  led anti-government demonstrations  against bashir's government but in past  months the coalition has been divided  that became the basis for the military  to stage a takeover in october placing  hamduck under house arrest and putting  members of his cabinet in prison a month  later he was released and then signed a  deal to form a government of technocrats  sidelining political groups when he  first took office hamdurk's popularity  was high among the protesters and when  he was placed under house arrest during  the military takeover many regarded him  as a symbol of civilian rule but the  deal he signed with the military in  november made him lose support of not  just the protest movement but also of  the political parties that brought him  to power  some activists say hamdok's resignation  could be in the interest of the protest  movement now that hamduk has stepped  down they realize that they need to get  their houses into order they need to get  there you know they need to get  everything organized they need to start  from scratch  and i think also the military side needs  to understand that the people will not  let up hamduck has cited lack of  consensus among political parties as his  reason for stepping down and as the  political parties remain at odds there's  little hope of both coming together to  name someone to replace him hiba morgan  al jazeera
 

